- **Increment T (2026-10-06) DONE**: the tie-pin trace shape reduction — the last named open item of the `MazeSearchAlgo::init` port. `ShapeSearchTree::change_item_shape(Item*, int, shared_ptr<TileShape>)` (Java `changeItemShapeUnlocked`: take the search-tree entries, remove only the old leaf from its shape slot, replace the `ItemSearchTreesInfo` precalculated shape for the same tree, rebuild the entries and re-insert) and `ShapeSearchTree::reduce_trace_shape_at_tie_pin(Pin*, PolylineTrace*)` (Java `reduceTraceShapeAtTiePin`: pin tree shape on the trace layer → first/last corner == pin center branch with shape index 0 / `corner_count()-2`, the 2-D intersection guard, `TileShape::cutout` pieces, keep the first 2-D piece or the piece containing the compare corner, then `change_item_shape`) are ported in `src/board/ShapeSearchTree.cpp`, with the new `Item::get_precalculated_tree_shapes`/`set_precalculated_tree_shapes` accessors in `src/board/Item.cpp`. `MazeSearchAlgo::init` now calls the anonymous-namespace `reduce_trace_shapes_at_tie_pins(set<Item*>, net_no, search_tree*)` for **both** start and dest item lists at the top of `init` (Java `MazeSearchEngine.init` lines 970-971), replacing the documented divergence comment; the helper only reduces foreign-net `PolylineTrace` contacts of `Pin`s with `net_count() > 1`. Java NPE cases (null pin shape on the layer) map to an early return + warning, as documented. 7 new gtests in the new `ShapeSearchTree_tie_pin_test.cpp` (change/keep tree consistency incl. the out-of-range guard, first/last-corner reduction, both no-op cases, null arguments) + 1 in `MazeSearchAlgo_test.cpp` (`InitReducesForeignTraceShapesAtTiePins`, foreign trace reduced / own-net trace untouched through `get_instance`) — **ctest 753/753 + run_tests PASSED** ✅. **Discovered latent bug (pre-existing, NOT fixed — not on this path)**: `TileShape::cutout` (`src/geometry/planar/TileShape.cpp`, the two dispatch branches where the hole is a `Simplex` and the dividing shape is an `IntOctagon`/`IntBox`) calls `divide->cutout_from(hole)`, producing hole-minus-divide (inverted vs Java `A.cutout(B)` = pieces of A minus B); every other dispatch branch is correct. Recorded in `03_MISSING.md` §2.1 and `MIGRATION_board.md`.
- **Increment U (2026-10-07) DONE**: the whole-plane `shape == null` free space expansion rooms. `ExpansionRoom.h/.cpp` adds the `WholePlaneShapeTag` internal constructor set (EMPTY shape + `is_whole_plane()` + board-box delegation) and the public ctor resize arm that turns a box grown to the board box into a whole-plane room; `AutorouteEngine.h` now only **forward-declares** `ExpansionRoom` (instantiation is in `.cpp`). `AutorouteEngine::complete_expansion_room` gains the `WholePlaneShapeTag` overload and the real overload rewrites the whole-plane null-shape case to `CompleteShapeInput.shape_type == NULL` with `IntBox::get_contained_box` (the Java `completeShapeUnlocked` null-start path) instead of the old bounded micro-box mapping. `MazeSearchAlgo.cpp` maze-start rooms and `ExpansionDrill::calculate_expansion_rooms` (drill rooms) both go through the whole-plane room; the interim identical-mixture containment guard is gone. **Parity consequence verified against Java**: a drill on an obstacle-free board now drops (the whole-board incomplete room completes to 4 `CompleteFreeSpaceExpansionRoom` pieces, never exactly one) — the 10 previously-green empty-board drill tests were reworked to restrained boards instead of "fixing" the drop (Java `DrillPage.getDrills` ~line 125 drops drills). Test rework: the `FakeObstacle` walls restored restrained rooms in `DrillPage_test`/`DrillPageArray_test`/`CompleteFreeSpaceExpansionRoom_test`/`MazeExpansionEngine_test`, with two real lessons — (1) `ShapeTree::insert` transfers leaf `unique_ptr`s to the object's `set_search_tree_entries`, so the fake must store them in a member (`search_tree_entries_`) or `MinAreaTree` dangles into a SIGSEGV (mirror of the board `Item::search_trees_info_` pattern); (2) `check_layer_with_any_matching_via` bails `NOT_DRILLABLE` when `search_->autoroute_engine()` is null, so `MazeSearchAlgo` got a public `set_autoroute_engine` (also used by `get_instance`). New parity tests: `CompleteFreeSpaceExpansionRoomTest.WholePlaneRoomCompletesToRestrainedFreeSpace` (wall → exactly one room `(0,0,4000,10000)`) and `WholePlaneRoomNeverCompletesToOneRoomOnObstacleFreeTree` (3-section split, `!= 1`), `MazeExpansionEngineTest.ExpandToDrillAddsElementForThickRoom`/`ExpandToDrillRejectsThinRoom` (sandwich walls → thin room `(0,470,10000,530)` `min_width()` 60)/`ExpandToOtherLayersAddsViaElementOnFreeSpaceDrill` — **ctest 755/755 + run_tests PASSED** ✅
- **Next**: the whole-plane rooms (`Increment U`) closed the last "tiny interim room" limitation. Next candidates: `RoutingBoard::autoroute_connection()` as a real board-level API (today `AutorouteEngine::autoroute_connection` carries the maze-first wiring, so the Java board facade API of the same name is still missing), the `fallbackToBoardVias` fanout via-rule combination (needs `RouterSettings::FanoutSettings` + `BoardRules::via_rules`), the `HeadlessBoardManager`/`ShapeSearchTree` drill-hole obstacle + clearance feature (Java `Via`/`Pin`/`Component` hole insertion), the `TileShape::cutout` Simplex-hole inversion bug (see Increment T), and the `PullTight*` quality paths.
- Parking lot note: WP-9's "rooms always created" simplification is now replaced by real reuse; room expansion/splitting around obstacles now uses `complete_shape` (Increment C), door creation from a room shape is ported (Increments E/F/G), the maze search that consumes those doors is ported (Increment I), the ripup costs of that search are ported (Increment J) and the trace shoving of that search is ported (Increment K). The connection location half of Phase 4 landed in Increment M; what is still missing is the insertion (Phase 4.4) and its engine rewiring.

