- **Test rework to Java parity**: `FakeObstacle` (net-2 wall, `is_trace_obstacle` true) + `ShapeTree::insert` walls restore restrained shapes in `DrillPage_test`, `DrillPageArray_test`, `CompleteFreeSpaceExpansionRoom_test` and `MazeExpansionEngine_test`. Two real lessons: (1) `ShapeTree::insert` transfers the leaf `unique_ptr`s to the object through `set_search_tree_entries`, so a **FakeObstacle must store them in a member** (`search_tree_entries_`) or `MinAreaTree` dangles into a SIGSEGV — the mirror of the board `Item::search_trees_info_` pattern; (2) walls are `IntBox(4000,0,6000,10000)` (⇒ contained rooms `(0,0,4000,10000)` / `(6000,0,10000,10000)`) and the sandwich walls `IntBox(0,0,10000,470)` + `IntBox(0,530,10000,10000)` with the drill at `(500,500)` produce the thin room `(0,470,10000,530)` (`min_width()` 60 < 100).
