### WP-10 Increment V: `RoutingBoard::autoroute()` board facade (2026-10-07)
- **Board-route facade (Java `RoutingBoard.autoroute(Item, RouterSettings, int viaCosts, Stoppable, TimeLimit)`, `board/facade/RoutingBoard.java:923-983`) is real.** Declared in `src/board/RoutingBoard.h` next to `fanout`, **defined in the autoroute module** (`src/autoroute/RoutingBoardAutoroute.cpp`) per the module-layering precedent from Increment R — the Java method needs `AutorouteControl` + `AutorouteEngine`, which the board module may not reference. Ported in full: the guard clauses (`NO_CONNECTIONS` for a null/inert item or an item with no net — the dead C++ `Connectable` is reproduced with the `is_trace()/is_via()/is_pin()/ConductionArea` guard already used by `calculate_target_doors`, see also `ExpansionRoom.cpp:212-222`), the `netCount > 1` warning, `ctrl_settings.remove_unconnected_vias = false`, the plane check (`CONNECTED_TO_PLANE` when the net contains a plane and the connected set holds a `ConductionArea`), the empty-destination `ALREADY_CONNECTED`, the local `AutorouteEngine` with `init_connection` (Java `init_autoroute(..., false)` always creates a fresh engine, so the local instance is equivalent), the maze-first `autoroute_connection` and the `ROUTED → opt_changed_area({net}, null, tracePullTightAccuracy, stoppable, null, 1000ms)` pull-tight call.
- **Prereqs ported in the same increment**: the `RouterSettings` cost shim is real — `get_via_costs()` returns `scoring_ ? scoring_->via_costs : 1` (was the `return 100` stub; the C++ `RouterScoringSettings::via_costs` int default 50 stands in for Java's null-contracted Integer, documented in the header, do not "fix" the scoring default), the `get_trace_cost_arr()` stub was replaced by a faithful `get_trace_costs()` plus the five per-layer accessors `get_preferred_direction_is_horizontal` / `get_preferred_direction_trace_costs` / `get_against_preferred_direction_trace_costs` / `get_horizontal_trace_costs` / `get_vertical_trace_costs` (Java `RouterSettings.java:638-649, 849-961`: out-of-range layer → warn + 0, missing array → 1.0). `AutorouteControl` gained the Java 5-argument ctor `(RoutingBoard*, net_no, RouterSettings*, via_costs, trace_costs)`; the existing 3-arg ctor now delegates to it.
- Tests: NEW `RoutingBoardAutoroute_test.cpp` (6 gtests: null item, non-connectable keepout `ComponentObstacleArea`, net-less pin, pin-on-plane `CONNECTED_TO_PLANE`, single-item net `ALREADY_CONNECTED`, two-pin net leaves the guard clauses and is handed to the maze search) → **ctest 761/761 + run_tests PASSED**.

